Committed as 2a7b9bf4. With YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1 set, the model's bash tool no longer receives the provider API key. Without it, nothing changes. Format, clippy and the full test suite all pass (6406 tests).

Real-binary probe: I ran the task's command against the built binary. With the variable set it printed len=0; without it, len=108. Both lines are in the commit body.

What changed:
• New `src/subprocess_env.rs` holds all the logic:
  • The switch turns on only for 1 or true (any case).
  • The list of variables to remove is yoagent's provider::api_key_variables() combined with yoyo's own provider table and the API_KEY fallback, with duplicates removed. GITHUB_TOKEN and GH_TOKEN are always kept so gh still works.
  • The removal happens only in the child process, so yoyo keeps its own key.
  • The module doc gives the reason it's opt-in: anyone who runs yoyo or another provider-calling tool from inside yoyo's bash needs the key, and my own evolve assessment does exactly that.
• `src/tools.rs`, +5 lines: a new scrub_vars field on the bash tool, empty by default. build_bash_tool fills it once per session, and it is applied just before the spawn.
• Docs: new section in docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md, new entry in ARCHITECTURE.md, and the tools.rs size-gate entry raised from 5207 to 5247. Only 5 of those 40 lines are mine; the file had already grown to 5242 within the allowed margin.

Tests (none set process-wide env vars):
• A canary command prints unset ghcanary with the scrub and canary ghcanary without it. A separate check confirms the canary really is in the unscrubbed output, so the test can't pass on an empty environment.
• A tool-level test scrubs HOME, which the test process already has, through the bash tool itself.
• Positive control: I disabled the apply_scrub call in tools.rs and restored it in the same command. Only the tool-level test failed, by name, and it went green again after the restore.

Not covered yet: sub-agent and explore-agent bash use yoagent's own bash tool, not build_bash_tool, so they still get the key. Hooks, /run, /bg, /watch and MCP stdio servers also still inherit it. EXA_API_KEY (web search, not a provider) isn't on the list. I posted all of these on #1064 with the commit sha, so the ticket's latest comment reflects the fix.
